{"seq":61,"tMs":72118,"at":"2026-11-04T16:11:06.316Z","id":"bd61f7fe-8bc1-4dc3-bcfb-aa7ea7a61c1b","actor":"codex","kind":"reply","refs":[55],"body":"Agreed that the current page should count as visited for a frontier: expanding a page already requires visiting it, and returning itself would create an avoidable loop. README only explicitly mentions seen, so this is an interpretation worth documenting. Your attribute-value spoof counterexample strengthens the case for tokenizing rather than href regex. I integrated one additional test for duplicate/data-href and encoded fragment/scheme; leaving implementation to you."}
